    <section class="workflow-card" id="prepare"><h2>How to prepare for an audit</h2><ol><li>Read the audit notice and evidence requests addressed to you.</li><li>Locate permitted digital references and authorized records.</li><li>Arrange physical originals for inspection when required.</li><li>Present evidence to the assigned auditor and track review feedback.</li><li>Review issued results and respond to required corrective actions.</li></ol><a href="/auditee/evidence-requests">My evidence requests</a></section>
    <section class="workflow-card" id="present"><h2>Present evidence without unnecessary copying</h2><p>Digital reference: provide an allowed code, location, or factual description. Omit restricted titles and identifiers. A file is not mandatory.</p><p>Physical original: record whether it is available or inspection needs arranging. The auditor records whether any required signature was actually verified.</p><p>Authorized upload: only copy a document if the owner and document-control rules permit storage here. Supported formats are PDF, DOCX, PNG, JPG, maximum 20 MB; files are encrypted privately. Never upload protected QMS materials solely because a request exists.</p><p>Illustrative example: “The signed original is available for inspection at the scheduled visit.” This is an availability statement, not a compliant decision.</p></section>
    <section class="workflow-card" id="respond"><h2>During-audit evidence and corrective evidence are separate</h2><p>During Audit responds to a specific request from your assigned auditor. Corrective Evidence responds to an open nonconforming check/CAR. Neither submitting evidence nor uploading a file changes N/C/O or closes a CAR.</p><p>Save a request response as a draft to resume later. Once submitted, wait for review or a request for additional information. Your notification history remains available offline through the application when you return; closed-app OS push is not supported.</p><a href="/auditee/my-findings?actionable=1">Actionable findings</a></section>
    <section class="workflow-card" id="nco"><h2>Understanding N / C / O</h2><p><strong>N — Non-Conformance:</strong> a requirement was not met. <strong>C — Compliant:</strong> the requirement was met. <strong>O — Observation:</strong> a factual observation recorded by the auditor.</p><p>Pending means unanswered, not a compliance result. The auditor makes these decisions from reviewed evidence. These are process assessments, not employee performance ratings. A finding and a CAR are separate from a checklist decision.</p></section>
    <section class="workflow-card" id="standards"><h2>Reference standards</h2><p>CompliTrack retains its existing ISO 9001:2015 internal-audit and ARTA reference identifiers. Ask the audit coordinator which approved criteria apply to your process.</p><p>No institutional retention period, filename rule, or classification scheme is imposed here. Approved external reference links and controlled-form reproduction require confirmation from the institution.</p></section>
